<title>UK: GWR passes the baton at Classic FM radio.</title>
<headline>GWR passes the baton at Classic FM radio.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>British radio operator GWR Group Plc said on Tuesday it had appointed a new managing director for its flagship commercial radio station Classic FM.</p>
<p>It has hired advertising agency director Murray Dudgeon from Universal McCann Worldwide, and he will take up his post on April 15, GWR said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
